=== Prompt for HW-006 (attempt 1) ===
Implement user story HW-006: Implement slugify() utility via Qwen/OpenRouter

## Story Description
Create slugify.ts in the project root. Export a single function `export function slugify(text: string): string` that lowercases the input, trims leading/trailing whitespace, replaces runs of whitespace or non-alphanumeric characters with a single hyphen, and strips leading/trailing hyphens (e.g. 'Hello,  World!' → 'hello-world'). Create slugify.test.ts with at least 5 vitest tests covering normal input, punctuation, repeated separators, leading/trailing whitespace, and empty string. Do not modify any existing files.

## Acceptance Criteria
- slugify.ts exists and exports slugify with correct signature
- slugify('Hello,  World!') returns 'hello-world'
- slugify('  Already-Slugged  ') returns 'already-slugged'
- slugify('') returns ''
- slugify.test.ts exists with at least 5 passing vitest tests
- tsc --noEmit exits 0
- vitest run exits 0 with all tests passing

## Technical Notes
- dependsOn: ["HW-001"]
- files: ["slugify.ts","slugify.test.ts"]

## Files to Create/Modify
slugify.ts, slugify.test.ts

## Dependencies
